[1mSymbol parity:[22m both libraries define exactly one dynamic symbol, [38;5;10mcrc16[0m. No macro-generated exports exist in [38;5;10mlib.h[0m (the header defines only typedefs, a [38;5;10mstatic[0m table, and the one prototype). [38;5;10mtests/symbols.rs[0m asserts this via [38;5;10mnm -D --defined-only[0m so it stays enforced.[0m[0m
