[1mOne harness defect I found and fixed:[22m my first version only built the Rust cdylib when it was missing. Because the lib target is [38;5;10mcdylib[0m-only, [38;5;10mcargo test[0m never rebuilds it, so the tests were loading a stale [38;5;10m.so[0m. A negative control — injecting [38;5;10m^ 1[0m into the tail loop — passed, which exposed this. The helper now runs [38;5;10mcargo build --lib[0m once per test process with the matching profile and feature set. Re-running the same injection fails 8 of 13 tests, and a second injection in the slice-by-8 path fails 8 as well, so the harness genuinely discriminates.[0m[0m
